# Build context exclusions for the deployment bundle images
# (deploy/docker/Dockerfile, built from the repository root).
#
# The server image installs its own dependencies and builds its own client
# artifact, so a developer's installed trees are never the right ones to copy in:
# node_modules holds a platform's native builds, vendor holds a dev-mode autoload
# map, and dist holds whatever was last built by hand. Excluding them also keeps
# the context small enough to send quickly.

.git
.github
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/vendor
**/dist
.pnpm-store

# A checkout's own environment files. The image is configured at run time from
# the deployment's env file, never from whatever the builder had lying around,
# and copying one in would bake a developer's secrets into a shipped layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Local state that must not enter a shipped image.
**/storage/logs/*
**/storage/framework/cache/data/*
**/storage/framework/sessions/*
**/storage/framework/views/*
**/storage/app/private/*
**/storage/app/public/*
**/.phpunit.result.cache
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.phpunit.cache

# Documentation, planning, and QA trees. The technician documentation the God
# Mode console serves is the packaged copy under
# apps/server/resources/technician-docs, which is committed; docs/ itself is not
# read at run time.
docs
scripts/process

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.claude
.idea
.vscode
